          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दिवाला",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिवाला — divālā — \"bankruptcy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उस दुकानदार का दिवाला निकल गया। us dukāndār kā divālā nikal gayā. That shopkeeper went bankrupt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिवाला (divālā) निकलना, to go bankrupt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिवाला (divālā) is filed by CDIAL under Sanskrit dīpāvali, \"a row of lamps\" (CDIAL 6358), beside दिवाली; how a row of lamps came to mean bankruptcy is not explained there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
